# {{ onboard_env | upper }} backend-operator bundle — {{ manifest.identity.name | default(operator_handle) }} ({{ operator_handle }})
Issued {{ ansible_date_time.date | default('see file mtime') }}. Hand-deliver; do NOT commit. Contains a private key.

You are a backend/admin operator on the {{ onboard_env }} goatnet. Full
orientation: docs/operations/admin-operator-guide.md.

## In this bundle
- operator-cert.pem / operator-key.pem  — your Zenoh operator leaf (CN {{ op_cn }}):
  writes the ops/** control + audit namespace.
- {{ onboard_env }}-ca-root.pem          — trust anchor for the {{ onboard_env }} router.

## 1. Install the cert
```
mkdir -p ~/.goat/{{ onboard_env }}-operator && cd ~/.goat/{{ onboard_env }}-operator
cp /path/to/this/bundle/{operator-cert.pem,operator-key.pem,{{ onboard_env }}-ca-root.pem} .
chmod 400 operator-key.pem
```
Zenoh TLS: root_ca_certificate={{ onboard_env }}-ca-root.pem,
connect_certificate=operator-cert.pem, connect_private_key=operator-key.pem,
endpoint {{ op_router_endpoint }}, enable_mtls=true.

## 2. Set your operator env
```
export GOAT_OPERATOR_HANDLE={{ operator_handle }}
export GOAT_OPERATOR_AGE_IDENTITY=~/.config/age/{{ onboard_env }}-operator.key   # your age private key
export {{ onboard_env | upper }}_PORTAL_OPERATOR_API_KEY='<your op_… key — see the operator who onboarded you>'
# Mint your OWN NetBird PAT (you have ADMINS): dashboard → Users → PATs → Create:
export {{ onboard_env | upper }}_NB_API_TOKEN='<your netbird PAT>'
```

## 3. What you can do
- Onboard a participant: `goat admin onboard <handle> --env {{ onboard_env }}`
  (mints NetBird key + Ory identity + Zenoh cert via the API/portal — no CA key needed).
- Revoke: `goat admin onboard <handle> --env {{ onboard_env }} --revoke`
- Rotate: `goat admin rotate <anchor|alias>`
- Read the admin audit: `goat audit ops`
- Admin consoles (MinIO/dashboard/isitup): log in — you have ADMINS{% if manifest.operator.groups is defined %} ({{ manifest.operator.groups | join(', ') }}){% endif %}.

## 4. Host shell
`ssh {{ op_host.ssh_user }}@{{ op_host.ssh_host }}`  (your SSH key is installed).

Keep operator-key.pem (0400) + your age private key safe. Your handle
({{ operator_handle }}) is what every admin action you take is attributed to.

